	{
		Title = "The Teamwork Update!",
		Subtitle = "2v2, Raid Bosses, and Battle Backgrounds!",
		Date = "December 22nd, 2023",
		Card = "TeammateDraw",
		["Patch Notes"] = { {
			Text = "\n2v2 AND 2v1 MULTIPLAYER IS HERE!\nYou will be able to join into a party with your teammate in the games menu, by forming a party, you will be able to play pretty much anything co-op, the only exceptions are City Trek and Puzzles. You can also Queue with a partner!\nWhen playing with a teammate, you will both share a baseplate, field and graveyard. Hands and Decks are separate!\nThe way turns work in this format is that one player on your team will take their turn, then the opponent will take their turn, then your second player on your team will take their turn, then the opponent, and so on.\nYou can also battle 2V1, too! Solo players will be given a special card to help make up for going up against two opponents, and we will be monitoring feedback to try to balance it out so that this style of play will still feel balanced.\nAs stated before, this mode is not limited to just Player Vs. Player Matches, you can also battle AIs with friends, Including a new type of AI we'll be adding with this update.\n\nRAID BOSSES!\nOn this update, you (and your partner!) will be able to face up against Zanzel, Perfected, a warped and twisted version of Zanzel who succeeded in her goals during Ancient Stirrings, Apocryphying the whole planet as well as herself.\nYou can access Raid Battles via the new Raid Event portal, located in the lobby.\nThis raid has two difficulties to it, Normal, and Extreme. You can choose which difficulty you would like to face.\nEach difficulty has its own set of rewards that you can potentially earn from completing the raid, including Apocryphic Sigils, a new event currency which can be spent at the event shop for various rewards!\n\nBATTLE BACKGROUNDS!\nOne of these rewards is a new type of cosmetic coming with this update, Battle Backgrounds!\nYou will now be able to choose between different backgrounds to appear while in the shop, deckbuilder, quest menu and in battle!\nCurrently we will only have the default and raid background available to choose, but we plan to add more purchasable ones in the future!\nyou can access this menu via the Cosmetics section in the shop!\n"
		} }
