	{
		Title = "Preparatory Balance Patch",
		Subtitle = "A small balance patch.",
		Date = "January 26th, 2024",
		Card = "Broken Dreams",
		["Patch Notes"] = { {
			Text = "For reasoning and other information, check our community server.\nThis is a small patch to address urgent issues; The first major balance patch of 2024 will release 3 weeks from now.\n\nRage: A mechanic change. Now only buffs the first attack with a rageborne this turn, rather than any fighter.\nThis stops the clown railgun (and all of its variants) and hopefully puts an end to the menace of this mechanic.\n\nRageborne Drill:\nEffect now \"During your end step, if you're in rage: Draw a card. You lose 500 life.\"\n2v2 rendered the old change redundant; I should've seen that coming.\n\nRageborne Bike:\nEffect now \"When this card is cast or during your end step, if you're in rage: Search your deck for 3 copies of this card. Unlock this card.\"\nThis kills the Bike OTK in 2v2 contexts.\n\nScribels:\nEffect now gives fighers that cost 1 more than the sacced card, rather than exactly the same cost or lower.\nNow that we have the tech to do this, goodbye titano cheese\n\nLua, Paraselene Evincar:\nEffect now \"If this card would take noncombat damage: Instead remove all ⚪ from all actions in your hand. Each action you cast this turn triggers its effect twice. You can't cast fighters this turn.\"\nThis stops the ultra annhilator combo and is honestly just a cleaner design. Technically a buff but like how much more degenerate can you get than LW OTK\n\n"
		} }
